<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alter Hof</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alter Hof is the former residence of the Wittelsbach dukes in the old town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, built from the mid-13th century. Emperor Louis IV the Bavarian made it the first permanent imperial residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. The dukes later moved to the new castle that grew into the Munich Residenz, and the Alter Hof was used for ducal administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alter-hof.jpg" alt="Alter Hof" width="320" height="578" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heribert Pohl --- Thanks for half a million clicks! from Germering bei München, Bayern · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%BCnchen,_Alter_Hof,_sp%C3%A4tgotischer_Torturm_und_Erker_am_Affenturm_(14282908665).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
